{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>These ten times</b> — The Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said: between Job's words and his companions' responses, they are now ten times. But the correct view in my eyes: it is like ואפו עשר נשים (and ten women baked), because the number ten is a round number."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as Saadia per standard epithet convention; his citation is confirmed by the explicit רב סעדיה in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:59.839475277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}